- # OpenStory
+ # ??
+
+ > Create 5-minute AI films with consistent characters. Iterate until you nail it. Open source and free to self-host.
+
+ ?? is an open source AI video production platform. Paste a script or a one-liner and it builds a multi-scene film with consistent characters and look — then you iterate until you nail it. Fully exportable, and free to self-host.
+
+ ## How It Works
+
+ 01. **Describe Your Idea**: Start with a one-liner or a full script. OpenStory builds out scenes, assigns characters and locations, and prepares shot directions for a multi-scene film.
+ 02. **Define Your Look**: Set your visual style, cast your characters, choose your locations. These carry across your entire project.
+ 03. **Generate & Refine**: Generate AI shots for every shot. Swap models, try variations, regenerate until every shot is right.
+ 04. **Export Everything**: Download shots, sequences, prompts, and music. Take it all into your editing tool of choice.
+
+ ## Features
+
+ - **From Idea to Finished Video**: Describe what you want in a line or paste a full script. OpenStory breaks it into scenes, generates shots, and scores the music — a multi-scene film with consistent characters, not a single-shot toy.
+ - **Cast Your Own Characters & Locations**: Define your characters and environments once — age, wardrobe, lighting, architecture. OpenStory maintains consistency across every shot in every sequence.
+ - **Get The Shot You Want**: Generate variations of any shot — different angles, lighting, compositions — and iterate the whole film until it’s exactly right.
+ - **Take Your Work Anywhere**: Download individual shots, export full sequences, and get the prompts behind every generation. Your work isn’t trapped here — use it in any editing tool or pipeline.
+ - **Latest Models**: Access the best image and video models as they ship. Switch per shot, or let OpenStory pick the best one for the job.
+ - **Music & Audio**: Generate music tracks and sound effects that match your sequence. Full audio composition built in.
+
+ ## Open & Fair
+
+ - **Open Source**: MIT licensed, full source on GitHub. Fork it, self-host it, or build entirely new workflows on top.
+ - **Bring Your Own Keys**: Use your own API keys or self-host entirely. Pay providers directly with no platform fees.
+ - **At Cost Pricing**: No subscriptions. AI usage at provider cost. A small fee applies only when buying credits.
+ - **Export Everything**: Shots, sequences, prompts, and music. Your work isn’t trapped — take it anywhere.
+
+ ## FAQ
+
+ ### What is OpenStory?
+
+ OpenStory is an open source AI video production platform. Paste a script or a one-liner and it builds a multi-scene film — consistent characters, locations, and look across every shot, up to around five minutes. Iterate on scenes until you nail it, then export. Free to self-host.
+
+ ### Do I need to write a full script?
+
+ No. You can start with a single line and OpenStory will expand it into a full script with scenes, characters, and shot directions. Or paste in a complete script if you have one.
+
+ ### What AI models does it support?
+
+ OpenStory fully supports the latest image and video models as close to day zero as possible. You can switch models per shot or let OpenStory pick the best one.
+
+ ### How does pricing work?
+
+ No subscriptions. Generations are billed at the rates of the labs and platforms that run them (fal.ai, OpenRouter, and more soon). A platform fee applies only when you buy credits, not on each generation. See openstory.so/pricing for the full model price list. Bring your own API keys to skip credits entirely.
+
+ ### Can I use my own API keys?
+
+ Absolutely. You can enter your own API keys directly — no self-hosting required. Pay providers directly with full control over costs and usage.
+
+ ### Is it open source?
+
+ Yes. MIT licensed, full source on GitHub. You can self-host it, fork it, or use the managed cloud version.
+
+ ### How do I get started?
+
+ Sign up to start immediately, or clone the GitHub repo to self-host. Describe your idea, define your look, and generate your first storyboard in minutes.
+
+ ## API
+
+ ?? has a public HTTP API for agents and scripts: create an AI video sequence from a script in one call then poll its status, or enhance a script on its own (streamed back). The endpoints below are self-describing and need no separate docs.
+
+ - API root (instructions, request schema, and HAL links): http://localhost:3000/api/v1
+ - OpenAPI 3.1 spec (JSON): http://localhost:3000/api/v1/openapi.json
+
+ Authenticate with an API key (create one under Settings → Developer) sent as "Authorization: Bearer <key>" or "x-api-key". POST /api/v1/sequences to create; GET the returned status URL (append ?wait=60s to long-poll) to watch progress. POST /api/v1/scripts/enhance to enhance a script without creating a sequence — the enhanced script streams back as Server-Sent Events.
+
+ ## MCP
+
+ MCP clients connect to http://localhost:3000/mcp (Streamable HTTP, protocol 2026-07-28, OAuth or an API key) to inspect a production, edit scenes, plan and approve generation, poll operations and export.
+ - Agent guide: http://localhost:3000/docs/developer-guide/agents
+
+ ## Documentation
+
+ - Docs: http://localhost:3000/docs
+ - Full docs (markdown): http://localhost:3000/docs/llms.md
+
+ ## Links
+
+ - Website: http://localhost:3000
+ - App: http://localhost:3000/
+ - GitHub: https://github.com/openstory-so/openstory
+ - License: https://github.com/openstory-so/openstory/blob/main/LICENSE
